WEBVTT

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.110
Two days have passed.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.300
Anne and Marilla are still deeply sad,

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.250
but they are slowly coming to
terms with Matthew's death.

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:43.390
And today, Matthew Cuthbert

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:52.520
has to leave Green Gables, where he
has spent all his life, forever.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.110
It would be troublesome to have
lunch when everyone has arrived.

00:01:58.120 --> 00:01:59.500
Why don't we have it now?

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.500
I don't feel like eating.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.100
That's no good. You have to eat something.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:07.880
Anne, it's me.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.100
Diana.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.080
Marilla, Diana is here.

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:12.900
Sorry to disturb you.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.970
I came a little early, as I thought I
could help out with some things.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:19.310
Father and mother will be here shortly.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:21.090
Sorry to trouble you, Diana.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.220
Thank you.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:31.440
To our bountiful Father above,

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:39.530
We will offer our tribute of praise

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:47.590
For the glorious gift of His love

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:55.020
And the blessings that hallow our days

00:02:55.560 --> 00:03:03.240
In the sweet by and by,

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:11.920
We shall meet on that beautiful shore

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:17.970
Amen

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:22.110
Well, it's time.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.250
If you please.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:28.530
Matthew leaves behind a home
filled with memories:

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:30.950
The trees which he has planted by himself.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.820
The orchard he has lavished great care on,

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:36.190
and the fields which he has plowed until now.

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.400
He is quietly escorted away.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:15.650
Nearer, my God, to Thee,
nearer to Thee!

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:29.440
E'en though it be a cross
that raiseth me;

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:43.720
Still all my song shall be
nearer, my God, to Thee,

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:58.380
Nearer, my God, to Thee,
nearer to Thee!

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:12.030
Though like the wanderer,
the sun gone down,

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:25.380
Darkness be over me,
my rest a stone;

00:07:25.940 --> 00:07:40.290
Yet in my dreams I’d be
nearer, my God, to Thee.

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:54.970
Nearer, my God, to Thee,
nearer to Thee!

00:07:54.970 --> 00:08:01.630
Amen

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:29.780
Well, it seems like there's
a lot of trouble ahead.

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:34.890
Is it true that the Cuthbert's
have lost all their savings?

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:37.270
It was a strike of luck

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:42.430
that you were able to work hard
and get that scholarship, wasn't it?

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:47.590
But I feel sorry for you. You'll have to
wear mourning clothes for a year.

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:51.630
Since you have red hair,
they won't suit you at all.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.110
They'll make your red hair
stand out even more.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:05.710
Soon thereafter, Avonlea settled back to its usual placidity.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:08.490
And as for Green Gables,

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:14.070
even though there's the aching sense
of "loss in all familiar things",

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:19.620
work is done and duties fulfilled with regularity as before.

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:16.890
Anne!

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:18.260
Diana.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:22.490
I was worried how you've been
getting on, but you look better now.

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:25.400
Say, do you want to come over to my place?

00:10:25.670 --> 00:10:28.710
The new sewing machine I asked my
father to buy has arrived today.

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:31.610
Oh my! A new sewing machine?
That's great!

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:36.140
Isn't it? That's why I came to get you.
I wanted you to be the first to see it.

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:41.630
Thank you. But unfortunately I have
to go to Matthew's grave now.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:42.980
Matthew's grave?

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:47.240
This rose was very important to Matthew.

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:49.610
Now that the roses are blooming so beautifully,

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:52.740
it would be a shame if Matthew couldn't
see them anymore, don't you think?

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:54.730
That's when I thought:

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:59.410
If I plant this beside his grave,
I'm sure Matthew will be pleased.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:05.980
Right. Then I'll go with you to the grave.
Then we can go to my place.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:07.470
Thank you, Diana.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:31.180
I heard Matthew's mother brought this
rose over from Scotland long ago.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:35.100
Matthew has taken good care of it.

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:38.370
He said this rose was his favourite.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:42.080
Every year, when this rose blooms,

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:46.110
Matthew will feel as though
he has returned to Green Gables.

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:19.320
It will be nice if it works.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:23.290
I hope that this rose will take root,

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:28.120
so that its cute flowers will
bloom every summer.

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:50.640
Say, Anne, what is Frank like?

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:52.060
What?

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:54.280
Didn't you say he's been going to school

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.910
with Josie since the day of
the entrance ceremony?

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:59.760
Oh, you mean Frank Stockley?

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:01.920
They happened to stay at
the same boarding house.

00:13:02.290 --> 00:13:05.740
Ruby told me something really funny.

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:10.200
A few days ago, Josie received a letter from Frank.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:14.200
Josie thought it was a love letter
and opened it excitedly.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.830
What do you think he had written?

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:17.300
What?

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:24.480
"I can't do my work. Please return
my workbook which you took by mistake."

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:25.970
That's all.

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:26.940
Oh dear!

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:33.960
Ruby told me that Frank
seems to like her, too.

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:36.710
I think Ruby stands a better chance.

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:40.730
In the past, whether it
was a lover or a boyfriend,

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:42.630
things have always gone smoothly for Ruby.

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:46.420
I'm sorry. I know it's rude
of me, but let's part here.

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:47.200
What's wrong, Anne?

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.030
It's not you, Diana.
Please don't take it to heart.

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:51.130
A-Anne!

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:53.250
I'm sorry!

00:14:17.510 --> 00:14:21.530
Anne doesn't know anything
about people dying,

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:24.760
and the events of the past
few days have been unexpected.

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:33.580
She thinks it almost sad that things can
go on in the old way without Matthew.

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:37.220
Nature, flowers, love and friendship

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:40.760
still arouse Anne's imagination
like they did in the past.

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:45.720
Anne realizes that she is still
capable of being touched.

00:14:46.210 --> 00:14:50.530
Different voices still exist in the world,

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:54.700
and they keep on calling out to Anne.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:59.580
Anne feels an embarrassment
that is similar to regret.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:05.770
My heart is filled with joy when I see
the sun rising behind the fir trees,

00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:09.390
and the pale, pink buds growing
day by day in the garden,

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:15.030
and everything seems to be the same
as when Matthew was around.

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:19.930
Matthew is already dead but I can
still feel excited by those things.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:22.500
I feel as though I've done Matthew wrong.

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:29.440
Matthew isn't here anymore,
and I miss him...all the time...

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:36.740
And yet, the world and life still
seem very beautiful and interesting to me.

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:42.790
Diana told me something funny today,
and I couldn't help but laugh.

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:51.410
When Matthew died, I thought
I could never laugh again,

00:15:52.170 --> 00:15:56.260
And it somehow seems as if I shouldn't.

00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:05.630
Anne, Matthew loved to hear you laugh
when he was around.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:12.770
When you were happy over something
interesting, wasn't he glad, too?

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:18.540
Matthew isn't here right now.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:24.390
I'm sure he still hopes to see you
happy and laughing like before.

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:29.480
I am sure we should not shut our hearts

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:33.590
against the healing influences
that nature offers us.

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:42.680
But I can understand your feelings. I think we all experience the same thing.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:51.370
When someone we love is no longer
here to share the pleasure with us,

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:56.530
we resent the thought that
anything can please us,

00:16:57.770 --> 00:17:02.730
and we almost feel as if
we were unfaithful to our sorrow

00:17:02.780 --> 00:17:05.810
when we find our interest
in life returning to us.

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:14.280
I planted a rose bush
on Matthew's grave this afternoon.

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:20.230
It was a cutting of the
little white rose that Matthew's mother

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:23.050
brought here from Scotland
a long time ago.

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:27.810
Matthew had said that that rose was his favourite.

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:34.370
They are so small and sweet,
blooming on their thorny stems.

00:17:35.480 --> 00:17:39.710
It made me feel glad that
I could plant it by his grave

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:41.640
as if I were doing something

00:17:41.650 --> 00:17:44.690
that must please him in taking
it there to be near him.

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:50.320
I hope he has roses like them in heaven.

00:17:51.130 --> 00:17:56.260
Perhaps the souls of all those little white roses,

00:17:56.630 --> 00:18:01.400
that he has loved so many summers,
were all there to meet him.

00:18:07.510 --> 00:18:09.670
I have to go.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:15.370
Marilla is alone at home, waiting for me.
She'll feel very lonely at twilight.

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:20.610
She'll be even lonelier still
when you go to university.

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:08.780
Marilla?

00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:13.310
I'm back, Marilla.

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:15.140
Welcome home, Anne.

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:21.880
When you were away, I met Dr. Spencer.

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:26.620
He said the eye specialist he mentioned
will be in Charlottetown tomorrow.

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:29.910
He said I must let him
examine my eyes thoroughly.

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:35.860
It would be nice if he could
prescribe you a good pair of glasses.

00:19:36.420 --> 00:19:39.900
Yes. I intend to make a trip anyway.

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:42.730
Can you take care of the house tomorrow?

00:19:43.000 --> 00:19:45.190
Yes. Of course, Marilla.

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:50.710
I'd like Martin to drive me there,
but there's ironing and baking to be done.

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:54.170
Don't worry. I shall attend to the
ironing and baking beautifully.

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:56.670
You needn't fear that I'll
starch the handkerchiefs

00:19:56.680 --> 00:20:00.040
or flavor the cake with liniment.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:04.590
Now that you mention it, that did happen before.

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:10.860
What a girl you were for making
mistakes in them days.

00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:14.200
You were always getting into scrapes.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:19.240
I seriously wondered what in
the world would become of you.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:21.720
Do you still remember the time
when you had your hair dyed?

00:20:22.270 --> 00:20:24.370
Yes, I remember that.

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:25.740
I couldn't forget that.

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:32.540
I laugh a little now sometimes when
I think what a worry my hair used to be to me.

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:35.250
But it was a very real trouble then.

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:38.720
I did suffer terribly over
my hair and my freckles.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:42.290
But now, the freckles are gone,

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:46.200
and everybody says
my hair is auburn now.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:48.740
All except Josie Pye.

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:55.040
On the day of the funeral, she said
my hair was even more red than before...

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:58.890
and that when I wore mourning clothes,
the redness stood out.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:04.280
Marilla, I've almost decided to give up trying to like Josie Pye.

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:08.550
I've made what I would once have
called a heroic effort to like her,

00:21:08.590 --> 00:21:10.750
but Josie Pye won't be liked.

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:17.860
Josie is a Pye, so she can't
help being disagreeable.

00:21:18.240 --> 00:21:22.780
However, I don't know what useful purpose
people of that kind serve in society,

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:26.230
any more than I know the use of thistles.

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:30.540
Does Josie intend to become a teacher, too?

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:34.070
No, she'll study for another year at Queen's.

00:21:34.120 --> 00:21:37.020
So will Moody Spurgeon and
Charlie Sloane.

00:21:37.490 --> 00:21:39.280
Jane and Ruby intend to become teachers.

00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:41.220
I see.

00:21:41.890 --> 00:21:44.320
Does Gilbert Blythe plan to become a teacher, too?

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:45.840
Yes.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.760
He's become a fine young man, don't you think?

00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:53.670
I hadn't seen him for some time.
He's grown taller and more manly.

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:56.850
He looks a lot like his father
did at the same age.

00:22:00.110 --> 00:22:03.910
John Blythe was a fine young man, too.

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:11.800
We used to be real good friends, he and I.
People called him my lover.

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:16.360
Oh, Marilla. And what happened?
Why didn't you...?

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:17.840
We had a quarrel.

00:22:20.230 --> 00:22:24.290
I wouldn't forgive him when he asked me to.

00:22:24.330 --> 00:22:27.960
I meant to, after awhile,

00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:33.600
but I was sulky and angry
and I wanted to punish him first.

00:22:34.480 --> 00:22:38.310
He never came back for me.

00:22:38.350 --> 00:22:42.770
I suppose the Blythes are
strong and independent.

00:22:50.390 --> 00:22:54.160
But I've always felt that I was wrong.

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:59.450
I wasted the opportunity for us
to forgive each other.

00:23:02.710 --> 00:23:06.040
So you did experience some romance in your youth, too.

00:23:07.310 --> 00:23:10.630
It's hard to imagine that
looking at me now, right?

00:23:11.180 --> 00:23:14.100
But you can't judge people by their looks alone.

00:23:14.850 --> 00:23:20.730
Everyone has forgotten about me and John.
Even I had forgotten about it.

00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:27.220
But everything came back when
I saw Gilbert Blythe the other day.

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:29.150
It doesn't feel too bad.

00:23:31.900 --> 00:23:34.270
Here you are, Marilla.

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:36.070
Thank you, Anne.

00:24:03.620 --> 00:24:06.670
Next on Anne of Green Gables:
Episode 49

00:24:07.030 --> 00:24:08.520
The Fork in the Road

00:24:08.530 --> 00:24:10.340
Please look forward to it!

00:24:14.530 --> 00:24:16.310
The Adventures of Tom Sawyer.

00:24:16.480 --> 00:24:18.700
Taking place in the grand nature surrounding Mississippi,

00:24:18.700 --> 00:24:22.180
Tom Sawyer and his friends
experience pleasant adventures.

00:24:22.410 --> 00:24:25.730
A wonderful world, full of dreams and hope.

00:24:26.170 --> 00:24:28.480
The new series 'The Adventures of Tom Sawyer'

00:24:28.480 --> 00:24:30.150
will start this spring!

00:24:30.150 --> 00:24:31.390
Please look forward to it!
